sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A video site's mark of its videos, read from the keywords of the page:
    YouTube's yt3d tags (yt3d:enable=LR, RL, LonR, RonL, true, false;
    swap; aspect; the left and right rectangles; malformed values read as
    far as they can be). The tags are read by libstereo-policy's site mark
    reader, the one reader the edition's programs share (PlasmaTube uses
    it too); the browser keeps no copy of its rules. The mark counts for a
    video whose stream and container carry none, after the stream's frame
    packing SEI and the container's mark, under the 3D Video menu's choice
    of the person and before the shape rule. A watch page's
    <meta name="keywords"> reaches its videos through a small actor
    (media.stereo.site-marks, on; media.stereo.site-marks.hosts, empty for
    every page).
  * The first form, yt3d:enable=true, is right eye first and yt3d:swap=true
    makes it left eye first, as YouTube's player took them (PlasmaTube's
    first patch had them the other way round).
  * The shape rule is libstereo-policy's: only a frame at least three
    times as wide as high is taken for side by side, so a 2.40:1 scope film
    stays flat.
  * Depends on libstereo-policy1 (>= 1.13.0), which has the site mark
    reader.
  * The source states what it is: SOURCE.edition.json (a quilt patch on the
    unchanged stereo3d5 orig tarball), debian/browser-build.env
    (MOZ_SOURCE_CHANGESET) and the vendor baseline name browser commit
    075e18be19b8a5f2fcc5b782c4392169a4c0eec0 (the stereo3d5 commit
    b1d115f8d3 plus the site mark patch).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

